\section*{Jiang–Su Embeddings in Character-Free Central Sequence Algebras}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
For nonzero unital separable C*-algebras, absence of characters in the norm central sequences is claimed to characterize Jiang--Su absorption; characterless algebras also have Jiang--Su-stable infinite minimal tensor powers. The cited manuscript argues for that result; its relation to this problem is specified below.

\subsection{Mathematical statement of the claimed result}
\paragraph{Mathematical claim 1.} For a nonzero unital separable complex $C^*$-algebra $A$ and free ultrafilter $\omega$, define its norm ultrapower $A_\omega$ and central-sequence algebra $F_\omega(A)=A_\omega\cap A'$, using the diagonal copy of $A$. OpenAI claims
\[
F_\omega(A)\text{ has no nonzero }*\text{-homomorphism to }\mathbb C
\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad A\simeq A\otimes_{\min}\mathcal Z,
\]
where $\mathcal Z$ is the Jiang--Su algebra. It additionally claims that for every nonzero unital separable characterless $D$, its infinite minimal tensor power $D^{\otimes_{\min}\infty}=\varinjlim(D^{\otimes n},x\mapsto x\otimes1)$ absorbs $\mathcal Z$ tensorially and admits a unit-preserving inclusion of $\mathcal Z$.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Manuscript 1 (family 299, 2026-09-25): Finite tensor labels detect noncommutativity in every representation and build a full square-zero element. Its two orthogonal corners are exactly equivalent, and a finite comparison absorbs their unit defect into a positive cutoff. This supplies dimension-drop maps; reindexed commuting copies then pass from the finite tensor construction to central-sequence absorption and infinite tensor powers.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
Manuscript 1 (family 299, 2026-09-25): The character criterion answers the central-sequence branch for nonzero unital separable A, and the infinite-power corollary handles separable D without characters; the extracted bundle omits these restrictions, so unrestricted nonseparable central-sequence absorption is not inferred.

\subsection{Formal verification}
For family 299, the scope page documents the following selections. The selection equates Jiang--Su absorption with absence of characters in the norm central-sequence algebra for nonzero unital separable algebras, without nuclearity or trace assumptions. The tensor-power consequence is separate. The documented statement covers the main claim of manuscript 1. It does not establish formal coverage of the complete problem clause. Comparator files: CharacterCriterion.lean. Declarations: OAI.KirchbergRordam.character\_criterion.

This site has not executed the Lean files or checked their dependencies. These descriptions report the scope of the linked declarations, rather than a new verification of the proofs.

\subsection{Status caveat}
OpenAI attributes these results to an internal model. Its release notice cautions that results lacking full formalization can contain mistakes. This site has not independently assessed the proofs; a solved label records the scope of the reported claim.

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item OpenAI, \emph{The Kirchberg–Rørdam character criterion}, 2026-09-25; citation key \texttt{OAI:The-Kirchberg-Rordam-character-criterion-September-25-2026}. \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/The-Kirchberg-Rordam-character-criterion-September-25-2026/paper.pdf}{PDF (GitHub)}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/raw/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/The-Kirchberg-Rordam-character-criterion-September-25-2026/paper.pdf}{PDF (direct)}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/The-Kirchberg-Rordam-character-criterion-September-25-2026/README.md}{Manuscript page and citation}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/main/preprints/The-Kirchberg-Rordam-character-criterion-September-25-2026/paper.pdf}{Latest version}; Statement source: \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/The-Kirchberg-Rordam-character-criterion-September-25-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex\#L70}{cor:infinite-tensor}; Statement source: \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/The-Kirchberg-Rordam-character-criterion-September-25-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex\#L37}{thm:main}.
\item Family 299: \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/lean/docs/299.md}{Lean scope}.
\item \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/lean/ComparatorChallenges/CharacterCriterion.json}{Comparator CharacterCriterion.json}.
\item \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/lean/ComparatorChallenges/CharacterCriterion.lean}{Comparator CharacterCriterion.lean}.
